originalText:
`insertSortedReferenceLine`'s doc (`generate.ts:252`) promises it returns `undefined` "when `rawText`'s `references` array isn't in the expected one-entry-per-line shape", but the only shape check is `REFERENCES_BLOCK_RE` matching `"references": [
…
]`. Given a root `tsconfig.json` whose entries are expanded (`{
  "path": "./scripts/a/tsconfig.build.json"
}` — valid JSON that prettier preserves), each physical line is treated as an entry, `extractEntryPath` returns `""` for the brace lines, and the comma-per-line rendering at `generate.ts:269` writes syntactically invalid JSON to the workspace root `tsconfig.json` with no post-write validation. Either verify one-entry-per-line before rewriting (bail to `rewriteRootTsconfig`) or re-`JSON.parse` the rendered text before writing.

evidence:
The function doc (line 252) promises it returns `undefined` when `rawText`'s `references` array isn't in the expected one-entry-per-line shape. However, the regex check at line 256 (`REFERENCES_BLOCK_RE.exec(rawText)`) only verifies the block exists in the `[
…
]` format. A tsconfig with expanded formatting (e.g., `{
  "path": "..."
}` per entry) would pass the regex, then `extractEntryPath` would return `""` for brace lines, and line 269 would render syntactically invalid JSON with commas on wrong lines.
